#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "&liloconfig;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this module, you can install lilo boot manager, add/remove/change boot "
"password, change time till booting default OS, add/remove/change default OS, "
"add/remove/change OS's, and more!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to organize all of these options, this module is divided into three "
"sections: <link linkend=\"lilo-general\"><guilabel>General Options</"
"guilabel></link>, <link linkend=\"lilo-OS\"><guilabel>Operating Systems</"
"guilabel></link>, and <link linkend=\"lilo-expert\"><guilabel>Expert</"
"guilabel></link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can switch between the sections using the tabs at the top of the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are not currently logged in as a superuser, you will need to click "
"the <guibutton>Administrator Mode</guibutton> Button. You will then be asked "
"for a superuser password. Entering a correct password will allow you to "
"modify the settings of this module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Options"
msgstr "Opcions generalas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From this page you can add/remove/change boot password, time till booting "
"default OS, and more!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Install boot record to drive/partition:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the drive or partition where you would like to install the Lilo boot "
"loader. Unless you intend to use other boot managers in addition to &lilo;, "
"this should be the MBR (master boot record) of your boot drive. In this "
"case, you should probably select /dev/hda if your drive is IDE, and /dev/sda "
"if your boot drive is SCSI."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boot the default kernel/OS after:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lilo will wait the specified time before booting default kernel/OS."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use linear mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Linear mode tells the boot loader the location of the kernels in linear "
"addressing rather than sector/head/cylinder. Linear mode is required by some "
"SCSI drives, and shouldn't hurt unless you are planning to create a boot "
"disk to be used with other computers. See lilo man file for more details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use compact mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The compact mode trys to merge read requests for adjacent sectors in to "
"single read request. This reduces load time and keeps boot map smaller, but "
"will not work on all systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "Record boot command lines for defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatic recording of boot command lines as defaults for following boots. "
"This way, lilo \"locks\" on a choice until manually overridden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrict parameters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A password is required only if any parameters changed (i.e. the user can "
"boot linux, but not linux single or linux init=/bin/sh). This sets a default "
"for all &Linux; kernels you want to boot. If you need a per-kernel setting, "
"go to Operating Systems tab, and select details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "Require password:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the password for bootup (if any) here. If restricted (above) is "
"checked, the password is required for additional parameters only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The password is stored in clear text in /etc/lilo.conf. You'll want to make "
"sure nobody untrusted can read this file. Also, you probably don't want to "
"use your normal/root password here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default graphics mode on text console:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select the default graphics mode here. If you intend to use a VGA "
"graphics mode, you must compile the kernel with support for frame buffer "
"devices. The ask setting brings up a prompt at boot time. This sets a "
"default for all &Linux; kernels you want to boot. If you need a per-kernel "
"setting, go to Operating Systems tab, and select details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter &lilo; prompt automatically"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is checked, lilo goes to the lilo prompt whether or not a key is "
"pressed. If it is turned off, lilo boots the default operating system unless "
"shift is pushed (in that case, it goes to the lilo prompt)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Operating Systems"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some of the things that can be done here are: settings like "
"<guilabel>General Options</guilabel> for specific kernels/OSes, set default "
"OS to boot, probe for available kernels, you can also edit root file system, "
"ramdisk settings, extra parameters, etc..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boot menu listbox"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To the far left is a list of the kernels and operating systems you can "
"currently boot. Choose the one you would like to edit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kernel:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the filename of the kernel you would like to boot. Pushing the "
"<guibutton>Select...</guibutton> will bring up &kde; standard fileselector "
"to help you find the kernel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Label:"
msgstr "Etiqueta :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the label (name) of the kernel you want to boot here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Root file system:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the root file system for the kernel you would like to boot. Pushing "
"the <guibutton>Select...</guibutton> will bring up &kde; standard file "
"selector to help you find the root file system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Root filesystem"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this case, the root file system means the partition that will be mounted "
"as / at boot time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Initial ramdisk:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use an initial ramdisk (initrd) for this kernel, enter its "
"filename here. Leave this field blank if you do not intend to use an initial "
"ramdisk for this kernel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Extra parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter an extra parameters you wish to pass kernel. Usually this can be left "
"blank. This can the append option in lilo.conf."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set Default"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boot this kernel if the user doesn't make a different choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Details"
msgstr "Detalhs"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "This brings up a dialog box with further, less commonly used, options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Probe"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automaticly generate a (hopefully) reasonable lilo.conf for your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run &lilo; in test mode to see if the configuration is ok."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Kernel..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add a new &Linux; kernel to the boot menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Other OS..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add non-&Linux; OS to boot menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove Entry"
msgstr "Suprimir l'entrada"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove entry from boot menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expert"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this page you can edit the /etc/lilo.conf file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do <emphasis>not</emphasis> edit this file so unless you know what you are "
"doing!"
msgstr ""
